# a-wave-of-twelve-miners — plan 23 K3, the CONTROL.
#
# Twelve miners into a sealed band, and the base is gone in ninety-four
# ticks.  It is the number its twin is measured against, and the twin
# differs from this file by ONE line.
#
# ── Read it beside its twin ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# `a-wave-screened-by-four.keys` is this file with
#
#     compose 0 12 miner      ->      compose 0 4 scout 8 miner
#
# and nothing else.  Same band, same wall, same spawn, same twelve
# robots, same tick loop.  Two thirds of that wave is still miners —
# and it never opens the wall at all.
#
# ⚠⚠ **That is the phase.**  A wave is as dangerous as its FASTEST
# class and no more: the four quickest robots in it fill the three
# hexes the approach fan reaches, and everything behind them is stood
# in a field.  `tests/23_k3_what_composition_is_worth.loft` measures the
# whole ladder; this pair is what it looks like being played.
#
# ── Why the list is AUTHORED as running ─────────────────────────
#
# `pending 0 0.0 15.0 on` (plan 18 S1b) starts the schedule where
# `a-base-that-plays-its-list.keys` drives a vehicle out to poke a
# spawn marker.  Both are real; this one keeps the run about the wave.
# A vehicle in the band is a second variable — it blocks, it salvages
# and it can be killed — and the twin has to differ in the composition
# and in nothing else.
#
# ── The world (identical to its twin) ───────────────────────────
#
#   five rows of grass, twenty-four columns:  (-3, -2) .. (20, 2)
#   sealed at q = 6 with a wall across all five rows
#   core at (0, 0), spawn at (14, 0) facing west
#
# ⚠ **Five rows, and the wall's ENDS are inside the fan here.**  The
# approach fan from (14, 0) lands on (6,-2), (6, 0) and (6, 1) — and
# (6,-2) is an END hex, worth 30 HP against a braced hex's 100 (plan 12
# B3).  That is why this band breaks at 35 ticks where a seven-row one
# needs 69: the fan is the same three hexes wide either way, and on a
# five-row wall one of the three is cheap.

echo twelve miners: a sealed band, and ninety-four ticks

do toggle_mode

# The core is where the target is.
do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

# The spawn, fourteen hexes east — clear of close_spawn_disable_radius
# (10) and well inside the scrambler bubble (25).
# ⚠ TWICE more: the place-kind cycle is spawn -> target -> tower ->
# spawn since plan 12 B5a gave towers a marker kind of their own.
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 14 0
marker 14 0 spawn 3

count markers 2 2
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -3 -2 20 -2
drag -3 -1 20 -1
drag -3 0 20 0
drag -3 1 20 1
drag -3 2 20 2
count painted 120 120

palette 9
click 6 -2
click 6 -1
click 6 0
click 6 1
click 6 2
kind 6 0 wall
count painted 120 120

# ── The wave, composed ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `schedule` arms a one-wave list and `compose` says what that wave is
# made of (plan 23 K1, `@X056`).  ⚠ The size is SUMMED from the parts
# and never stored, so `schedule 12` followed by `compose 0 12 miner`
# is a wave of twelve because the parts say twelve — not because the
# two lines agree.
schedule 12
compose 0 12 miner
pending 0 0.0 15.0 on
waves 0 0
count alive 0 0

# ── The wave goes out on the next tick ──────────────────────────
#
# A wave spawns STACKED on its marker hex and leaves one enemy per
# tick, so `range` is a span rather than a point.
tick 1
waves 1 1
count alive 12 12
enemy 0 14 0

# ── Nine ticks: standing, and the wall is untouched ─────────────
#
# The pre-walk window is 8 ticks (plan 16 W2) and a standing enemy
# chews nothing whatever its class.  The braced middle is 100 HP and
# both ends are 30 (plan 12 B3).
tick 9
hp 6 0 100.0 100.0
hp 6 -2 30.0 30.0
count targets 0 0

# ── Thirty ticks: the siege is on, and it is on THREE hexes ─────
#
# ⚠⚠ **Three, on a wall that is five wide** — the front is the approach
# fan's width, not the wall's, and widening the band to seven rows does
# not add a fourth (measured in `23_k3`).  So a wave's usable width is
# three, and this is the whole reason its twin exists: four robots is
# enough to own the lot.
tick 20
count targets 3 3
target 0 6 0
hp 6 -2 9.5 10.5
hp 6 0 77.0 79.0
hp 6 -1 100.0 100.0

# ── And through ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The cheap end goes first, at 3.0 HP/s a miner against 30 HP with
# nothing to lean on, and the breach is the way in.
tick 5
kind 6 -2 grass
count painted 120 120

# ── The clock ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ Ninety-four ticks from the arming of the list to a drained wallet.
# Its twin is still standing at 321 — the longest base anybody can play
# (`@M005`) — with the wall unopened.
fall 200
ticks 90 100
wallet 0.0 0.0

snap k3-twelve-miners-are-through
